title: "When AI Begins to Build Itself: An Academic and Didactic Analysis of When AI Builds Itself"
type: report
authors:
  - family-names: "Silva"
    given-names: "Aridio"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-2411-6995"
date-released: "2026-09-08"
version: "1.0.0"
license: "CC-BY-4.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/aridiosilva/ai-builds-itself"
abstract: >-
  An independent academic and didactic analysis of the Anthropic Institute
  article When AI Builds Itself. The work distinguishes AI-accelerated
  research and development from full recursive self-improvement, evaluates
  the evidence and its limitations, and discusses implications for scientific
  practice, human expertise, AI safety, and governance.
keywords:
  - artificial intelligence
  - autonomous agents
  - recursive self-improvement
  - automated AI research
  - AI governance
  - AI safety
  - human oversight
  - research automation
